      en: "Manaslu is the eighth highest mountain in the world at 8,163 meters. It is located in the Mansiri Himal, part of the Nepalese Himalayas. Its name is derived from the Sanskrit word 'Manasa', meaning 'Mountain of the Spirit'. The mountain is known for its variable weather and high risk of avalanches. The first ascent was made by a Japanese expedition in 1956, which is why the mountain holds special significance for Japanese climbers and is sometimes referred to as the 'Japanese mountain'. The Manaslu Circuit is a popular trekking route, offering breathtaking views and an insight into the region's Tibetan-influenced culture. The Manaslu Conservation Area was established to protect the unique flora and fauna of the region."
